<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cad0c476-d7cd-4c43-bbe7-2be705b8c29c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cad0c476-d7cd-4c43-bbe7-2be705b8c29c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "D8: Case restoration by shared-prefix copy" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cad0c476-d7cd-4c43-bbe7-2be705b8c29c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/20157892-bc76-4766-9c99-df01009eb71b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cad0c476-d7cd-4c43-bbe7-2be705b8c29c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cad0c476-d7cd-4c43-bbe7-2be705b8c29c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Lookup key: ASCII lower-casing into a 64-byte stack buffer; allocating to_lowercase only for long or non-ASCII words. Output: copy the input's characters over the shared lower-cased prefix (ISBNs→ISBN, Territories→Territory); Title Case in gives Title Case out (Mice→Mouse, Person→People); for all-caps input, rewritten letters are upper (MOUSE→MICE, TERRITORY→TERRITORIES) and a purely appended suffix is lower-case per the acronym convention (ISBN→ISBNs, ID→IDs, BOX→BOXes)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cad0c476-d7cd-4c43-bbe7-2be705b8c29c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cad0c476-d7cd-4c43-bbe7-2be705b8c29c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T18:43:50.928102Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
